          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Dedekind completion
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+order"} linear order
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is a new strict linear order
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi L
                    %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widebar{L}
            that contains
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suprema"} suprema
            for all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+subsets"} bounded subsets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is still a supremum in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi L
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widebar{L}
          %p
            While Dedekind completeness was traditionally described in the context of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+linear+order"} strict linear order
            %span.newWikiWord
              dense
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/dense+order"} ?
            and unbounded (without
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/top"} top
            or
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bottom"} bottom
            %em Dedekind complete
            if
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+cuts"} Dedekind cuts
            don’t give any ‘new’ elements.
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            equipped with the structure of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+linear+order"} dense linear order
            without
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/top"} top
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bottom"} bottom
            elements (endpoints).
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong cut
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is a pair of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L, U \subset S
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              that satisfy the following eight properties:
            %ol
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                is
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+subset"} inhabited
              %li
                Dually,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                is inhabited;
              %li
                If
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi L
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \lt y \in L
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi L
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in L
              %li
                Dually, if
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo &gt;
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \gt y \in U
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in U
              %li
                If
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi L
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in L
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \lt y \in L
                for some
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              %li
                Dually,
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in U
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mi y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \gt y \in U
                for some
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              %li
                If
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \lt y
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in L
                or
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in U
              %li
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in L
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in U
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo &lt;
