          %h2#generalisations Generalisations
          %h3#in_predicative_constructive_mathematics In predicative constructive mathematics
          %p
            In predicative constructive mathematics, subsets are large and therefore are proper classes. Thus, any Dedekind completion of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+linear+order"} dense linear order
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+class"} proper class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mi to
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L, U: \mathbb{Q} to \Sigma
            representing the open subsets of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            to define
            = succeed "," do
              %strong predicative cuts
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            is a small
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-frame"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              \-frame
            with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding"} embedding
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                    %mi 𝒰
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma \to \mathrm{Prop}_\mathcal{U}
            into the large set of propositions for a universe
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒰
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              Given a small
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-frame"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                \-frame
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              that embeds into the large set of propositions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                      %mi 𝒰
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Prop}_\mathcal{U}
              for a universe
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒰
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
              and a linearly ordered set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %strong cut
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is a pair of functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo :
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L, U: S \to \Sigma
              that satisfy the following eight properties:
            %ol
              %li
                There is an element
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in S
                such that
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo ⊤
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(a) = \top
              %li
                There is an element
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in S
                such that
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo ⊤
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(b) = \top
              %li
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \lt b
                are elements of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                with
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo ⊤
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(b) = \top
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo ⊤
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(a) = \top
              %li
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \lt b
                are elements of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                with
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo ⊤
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(a) = \top
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo ⊤
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(b) = \top
              %li
                If
